{"findings":[{"claim":"Agy reader classification misses commands whose first word is a launcher wrapper (sudo, env, nohup, su, doas, start) and pipe-only chains: command_shaped requires the first whitespace word to be in AGY_COMMAND_WORDS and only treats &&, ||, ;, > as chaining, so a Scanned string such as 'sudo rm -rf x' or 'cat f | sh' under an unknown key is judged not-writing.","evidence":[{"kind":"read-code","observation":"command_shaped checks first_word against AGY_COMMAND_WORDS (rm, git, powershell, ...) and chaining only for &&, ||, ' > ', '>>', ';' + command word; sudo/env/nohup absent, single '|' absent.","reference":"crates/c3/src/engines/tree_check.rs:303-330, 352-401"}],"locations":[{"line":306,"path":"crates/c3/src/engines/tree_check.rs"}],"remedy":"Normalize launcher prefixes (strip sudo/env/nohup/doas/su/runas/start) before first-word test and treat '|'/$()/backticks as chaining, or scan every whitespace word for a command word.","severity":"major","supersedes":[],"trigger":"An allow-listed reader logs a parameter under an unknown key with value 'sudo rm -rf x' or 'cat f | sh' and the tree changes.","verification":"Unit-test agy_params_show_write on those two strings under an unknown key and assert true."},{"claim":"No-hardlink patch placement can take over a live owner's claim: an EMPTY claim unchanged for 60 s is Abandoned and removed/re-claimed, but a live owner stalled >60 s between exclusive create and rename (AV, suspend, slow FS) still holds its tmp; the taker's rename then wins and the owner's later rename replaces or fails against the taker's file.","evidence":[{"kind":"read-code","observation":"reuse_patch returns Abandoned for empty file with mtime age >= claim_stale_after (60 s); place_without_link claims via create_new then rename; drop_own_claim only protects the failing renamer, not the stalled owner whose rename runs second.","reference":"crates/c3/src/consult/reviewed.rs:1125-1201, 1249-1298"}],"locations":[{"line":1125,"path":"crates/c3/src/consult/reviewed.rs"},{"line":1258,"path":"crates/c3/src/consult/reviewed.rs"}],"remedy":"Hold the claim open (keep the create_new handle alive until rename) or re-check identity after rename; extend the 60 s window and log both pids.","severity":"major","supersedes":[],"trigger":"Two concurrent --diff placements on one patch name where the first stalls >60 s between claim create and rename.","verification":"Hold patch-claim race point >60 s in one process, start a second placement, then release the first and inspect which bytes survive."},{"claim":"open_patch_dir creates the outside-repo collab anchor by pathname before any handle check: when the collab root lies outside the repo, create_dir_all(collab_root) follows links above it, so a link above the anchor defeats the contained-from-handle guarantee that covers the in-repo case.","evidence":[{"kind":"read-code","observation":"open_patch_dir: in-repo branch anchors on repo_root; outside branch does std::fs::create_dir_all(collab_root) by path, then Root::open_anchor(collab_root); only components below the anchor are opened without following.","reference":"crates/c3/src/consult/reviewed.rs:1300-1340"}],"locations":[{"line":1319,"path":"crates/c3/src/consult/reviewed.rs"}],"remedy":"Resolve/create the outside anchor through handles too (create missing parents via Root or refuse when the anchor or a parent is a link).","severity":"minor","supersedes":[],"trigger":"--collab-dir outside the repo whose parent chain contains a symlink/junction when a --diff patch is placed.","verification":"Point --collab-dir at an outside path under a swapped link parent and trace where the handoffs dir is created."},{"claim":"Death-record newest-stream rule decides by filesystem mtime with second-granularity ties broken toward the note: on filesystems with coarse mtime or equal timestamps the pending main stream can still win over a newer continuation, and a missing noted file falls back to the note even when the pending file is the newer evidence.","evidence":[{"kind":"read-code","observation":"noted_stream_wins compares mtime(pending) vs mtime(noted), n>=p wins; (Some,None)=>false, _=>true; tie goes to note; test sleeps 50 ms to separate mtimes.","reference":"crates/c3/src/consult/detach.rs:1206-1238"}],"locations":[{"line":1206,"path":"crates/c3/src/consult/detach.rs"}],"remedy":"Compare (mtime, size/hash) or sequence numbers from the status note instead of mtime alone; document tie behavior.","severity":"note","supersedes":[],"trigger":"Main and continuation streams created within one mtime tick, or the noted continuation file already pruned.","verification":"Create both streams with identical mtimes and check which events_file the death record keeps."}],"first_run_checklist":[],"prior_findings":[{"id":"F02-1","note":"Read-only review, no commands run.","status":"not-checked"},{"id":"F02-2","note":"Read-only review, no commands run.","status":"not-checked"},{"id":"F02-3","note":"Read-only review, no commands run.","status":"not-checked"},{"id":"F02-4","note":"Read-only review, no commands run.","status":"not-checked"},{"id":"F02-5","note":"Read-only review, no commands run.","status":"not-checked"},{"id":"F02-6","note":"Read-only review, no commands run.","status":"not-checked"},{"id":"F02-7","note":"Read-only review, no commands run.","status":"not-checked"},{"id":"F02-8","note":"Read-only review, no commands run.","status":"not-checked"},{"id":"F02-9","note":"Read-only review, no commands run.","status":"not-checked"},{"id":"F02-10","note":"Read-only review, no commands run.","status":"not-checked"},{"id":"F02-11","note":"Read-only review, no commands run.","status":"not-checked"},{"id":"F02-12","note":"Read-only review, no commands run.","status":"not-checked"},{"id":"F02-13","note":"Read-only review, no commands run.","status":"not-checked"},{"id":"F02-14","note":"Read-only review, no commands run.","status":"not-checked"},{"id":"F02-15","note":"Read-only review, no commands ru